</p>
<p>The twins must be either the mother and her brother or the son and daughter. Either way, they are of opposite genders. This means that the winner and the loser are of the same gender. These two can&#8217;t be the mother and daughter, because they must be the same age. That means they&#8217;re the son and brother. The son can&#8217;t be the winner, because that would require that the brother&#8217;s twin (the mother) be the same age as the son. So the only possibility is that the brother won the tournament.</p>
